1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,871
Part two.

2
00:00:01,231 --> 00:00:02,891
The trillion-pound baby.

3
00:00:03,796 --> 00:00:05,317
Marcus has a favorite joke.

4
00:00:05,631 --> 00:00:08,208
A father tweets that his baby doubled its

5
00:00:08,255 --> 00:00:09,114
weight in a month,

6
00:00:09,474 --> 00:00:11,180
and projects that by college,

7
00:00:11,204 --> 00:00:13,340
the kid will weigh a trillion pounds.

8
00:00:14,245 --> 00:00:15,128
Growth like that,

9
00:00:15,174 --> 00:00:17,670
Marcus says, always tails off.

10
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:20,492
And he thinks Anthropic's already has.

11
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,024
In the second quarter,

12
00:00:22,279 --> 00:00:24,729
revenue grew 147%,

13
00:00:24,752 --> 00:00:27,411
during what he calls the token-maxing fad,

14
00:00:27,643 --> 00:00:29,814
when companies told staff to use as much

15
00:00:29,907 --> 00:00:31,312
AI as they could.

16
00:00:31,672 --> 00:00:32,879
In the third quarter,

17
00:00:33,076 --> 00:00:35,062
growth was 47%.

18
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,256
Then there's competition.

19
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:40,193
Since 2023, he has argued that everyone is

20
00:00:40,263 --> 00:00:41,679
building the same thing,

21
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:43,908
which means price wars.

22
00:00:44,338 --> 00:00:46,730
Cheaper Chinese models made that real this year,

23
00:00:46,765 --> 00:00:50,039
he says. That leaves Anthropic one niche:

24
00:00:50,398 --> 00:00:52,163
the very top-end models.

25
00:00:52,523 --> 00:00:55,216
Host Alex Kantrowitz put it this way:

26
00:00:55,785 --> 00:00:58,386
if an associate professor can do the job,

27
00:00:58,746 --> 00:01:00,395
why pay the full professor?

28
00:01:00,824 --> 00:01:02,763
And each step up costs more.

29
00:01:03,251 --> 00:01:05,991
One billion to impress users this year,

30
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,998
Marcus warns, ten billion next year,

31
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:11,006
a hundred billion after that.

32
00:01:11,436 --> 00:01:13,270
Kantrowitz added more pressure:

33
00:01:13,758 --> 00:01:16,893
five customers make up 19% of revenue,

34
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,261
and some big ones are pulling back.

35
00:01:20,039 --> 00:01:23,975
Marcus's conclusion: Anthropic has to stay a rocket.

36
00:01:24,462 --> 00:01:27,434
Every customer who pulls back makes escape velocity

37
00:01:27,515 --> 00:01:29,466
harder. That's the bear case.

38
00:01:29,501 --> 00:01:31,811
Now meet the man who thinks it's wrong.
